Changelog: 21-11-2026 19:51:41

Added. Ethernet First, a new quickfix: it turns the Wi-Fi off while a network cable is connected, and on again when
the cable is gone. Turn on installs a NetworkManager hook and a timer that checks the cable 45 seconds after boot.
The hook turns on only a Wi-Fi it turned off itself. Turn off removes both and turns that Wi-Fi on again.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 12:04:44

Release 0.5.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 11:51:00

Added. Boot Command Line has one row of five even places: its boxes, Read and Save. Save changes is Save now, with Your
changes under it, and the question's title says Save. The list of command lines is above the table, labeled Command
line, and wide enough for every name. The captions are New row under Add, Selected row under Remove, Revert changes
under Revert and Explain under Settings, which was All settings. The window has one info symbol: the second one's
text about the boot partition is a chapter of the first. Settings lists the arguments in six chapters with a heading,
each argument's name on its own line and its values as a list. MangoHud Config's Revert says Revert changes too.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 10:40:50

Added. Every quickfix's window is a card now, core's template (owner, 21-11-2026). The Refresh pill is gone: a round
refresh symbol of the info symbol's size sits at the right end of the title row, and no pill stands in that row. The
boxes and pills are all as wide as the widest, five on a row at most, and the window is as wide as a full row. A
switch has its boxes, Turn on and Turn off on one row. A switch with four boxes has Turn on and Turn off on a second
row. MangoHud Config has its boxes, Revert and Save on the first row and the FPS log's pills on the second, and its
Delete old logs pill is Delete logs. Tools is the exception: its group pills stay on the left at their own width, with
each group's tools beside its pill instead of under it. Boot Command Line has its boxes and the file list on the first row and Read and Save
changes on the second.

